WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
In 1929, an English
mathematician turned philosopher,

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.180
Alfred North Whitehead,
published a bold idea.

3
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:11.920
The world, he said, is
not made of fixed things.

4
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.550
It is made of events,
moments of experience.

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.580
From that idea grew process theology.

6
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.940
Some Christians who follow it
believe God cannot do everything,

7
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.790
and did not create the world from nothing.

8
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.700
What kind of God is that?

9
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.910
In this mission, you'll meet
the process picture of God,

10
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.920
and what it says about
evil and about death.

11
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.690
Then you'll weigh up whether
this God is the Christian God.

12
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.030
Your mission: find out what process
theology says about God's power,

13
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.310
creation and life after death.
